# Native Siphon app (`mac/`)

- SwiftUI, macOS 26, bundle id `com.machiilabs.siphon`; `mac/project.yml` (XcodeGen) is the source of truth. The `.xcodeproj` and `Info.plist` are generated and gitignored.
- Build only with `bash mac/scripts/build_and_install.sh`: it bumps `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`, builds Release, runs the unit tests, and prints `✓ Siphon <version> (<build>)`. Report that line.
- `--integration` also runs `IntegrationTests` (a real yt-dlp download of the iStock sample into `/tmp`); run it after engine changes.
- `/Applications/Siphon.app` is still the web version's launcher. Don't pass `--install` (and never `--replace-web-launcher`) until the user says the native app replaces it.
- The app reads the repo's `sites/` folder (copied into the bundle at build time), so site entries work in both versions.
- Views get `DownloadQueue` as an explicit parameter, not through the environment (same rule as Skagway).
- Don't drive the GUI; hand the user repro steps instead.
